  "description": {
    "raw": "This spell functions as reincarnate except that you can cause the new body to resemble a particular creature, matching its age category and sex and rerolling any race result that would be the wrong size category. The subject further gains a +5 bonus on Disguise checks to impersonate the chosen creature due to similar features, although it might take a penalty for being the wrong race.\n\nThe spell automatically leaves you with a small piece of the creature’s new body, typically a lock of hair (useful for scrying and other such spells).",
    "search_text": "\"this spell functions as reincarnate except that you can cause the new body to resemble a particular creature, matching its age category and sex and rerolling any race result that would be the wrong size category. the subject further gains a +5 bonus on disguise checks to impersonate the chosen creature due to similar features, although it might take a penalty for being the wrong race.\\n\\nthe spell automatically leaves you with a small piece of the creature’s new body, typically a lock of hair (useful for scrying and other such spells).\"",
